Check that the time zone fits before appending it to the
format.POSIXlt() output buffer.

do_formatPOSIXlt() (src/main/datetime.c) fills a 2049-byte stack
buffer with strftime(buff, 2049, ...) and then, for usetz = TRUE,
strcat()s " " and the zone name with no length check.  A format whose
output is 2045 to 2048 bytes writes the zone past the end of the
buffer, and a long "zone" component or "tzone" attribute, both
user-settable, writes any number of bytes past it.  Compute the
appended length and signal the existing "output string exceeded 2048
bytes" error when the result would not fit.

The strcat() calls date from 2001 and 2013; until r83243 (R 4.3.0)
the buffer was 300 bytes with a 256-byte strftime() limit, so a short
zone always fit and only the long-zone case overflowed.

Found by OSS-Fuzz (afl_asan_r, datetime): testcase 4835518689640448,
a stack-buffer-overflow WRITE of 4 bytes from a 2045-byte literal
format with usetz = TRUE in Europe/London.

Upstream status: r-devel/r-svn PR #457 and Bugzilla PR#19291, filed
2026-11-07.  The upstream PR also adds a regression test to
tests/reg-tests-1e.R, left out here so this carry patch does not go
stale with that file.
Delete this patch once the fix lands in R trunk.

diff --git a/src/main/datetime.c b/src/main/datetime.c
index 214f22f039..5a4430c7c3 100644
--- a/src/main/datetime.c
+++ b/src/main/datetime.c
@@ -1451,13 +1451,14 @@ attribute_hidden SEXP do_formatPOSIXlt(SEXP call, SEXP op, SEXP args, SEXP env)
 		Rf_error("output string exceeded 2048 bytes");
 	    }
 
-	    /* Now assume tzone abbreviated name is < 40 bytes,
-	       but they are currently 3 or 4 bytes.
-	    */
+	    /* Time zone abbreviations are currently 3 or 4 bytes, but
+	       both the "zone" component and the "tzone" attribute can be
+	       set by the user, and the strftime output may already have
+	       filled buff, so check the appended length fits. */
 	    if(UseTZ) {
+		const char *p = NULL;
 		if(have_zone) {
-		    const char *p = CHAR(STRING_ELT(VECTOR_ELT(x, 9), i%nlen[9]));
-		    if(strlen(p)) {strcat(buff, " "); strcat(buff, p);}
+		    p = CHAR(STRING_ELT(VECTOR_ELT(x, 9), i%nlen[9]));
 		} else if(!isNull(tz)) {
 		    int ii = 0;
 		    if(LENGTH(tz) == 3) {
@@ -1465,8 +1466,14 @@ attribute_hidden SEXP do_formatPOSIXlt(SEXP call, SEXP op, SEXP args, SEXP env)
 			else if(tm.tm_isdst == 0) ii = 1;
 			else ii = 0; /* Use base timezone name */
 		    }
-		    const char *p = CHAR(STRING_ELT(tz, ii));
-		    if(strlen(p)) {strcat(buff, " "); strcat(buff, p);}
+		    p = CHAR(STRING_ELT(tz, ii));
+		}
+		if(p && *p) {
+		    size_t len = strlen(buff), plen = strlen(p);
+		    if(len + 1 + plen >= sizeof(buff))
+			Rf_error("output string exceeded 2048 bytes");
+		    buff[len] = ' ';
+		    memcpy(buff + len + 1, p, plen + 1);
 		}
 	    }
 	    SET_STRING_ELT(ans, i, mkChar(buff));
